; BOUNCE BONANZA - song 1, course 1 "First Roll": "Fairway" (SPEC.md 128.20)
;
; G major at 117 BPM, a gently SWUNG shuffle: a 16th is a row, and the rows
; alternate eight and six sub-ticks (`groove 8 6`), so an 8th is always 14
; and every off-beat 16th lands a little late - the lilt of a putt rolling
; across a lawn. A pattern is two bars of 4/4, 4.1 s.
;
; The harmony is a ragtime lawn-party's: I - VI7 - II7 - V7 (G E7 A7 D7),
; the secondary dominants walking round the circle of fifths back home. The
; accompaniment is an oom-pah: the plucked bass on beats 1 and 3 with a
; swung 16th pickup, the harp's chord on 2 and 4.
;
; The intro is a two-bar vamp on A7 - D7: the recorder hops (a note, a gap,
; a note) like a ball being tapped onto the green, then strolls up into the
; tune. A's MOTIF is a skip and a push - down a third, back up and HELD over
; the swung "a", up to a chord tone, then a dotted step down to rest:
;   d8 b16 d16&d8 g8 | e8. d16 b4      (over G)
; stated three times climbing the circle (G, E7, A7) and answered by a long
; question on D7 (A). The second A climbs once less and cadences with a run
; up to the tonic, which the chiparp sparkles. B, the bridge, turns to the
; GLOCKENSPIEL over a half-time beat and a falling bass (C B A D): a broad,
; bouncing figure - a note, down a third, back, up a fourth - sequenced down
; the chords, and a D7 run that spills back into A. Intro, A A' B A' for ever.
;
; THE SPEAKER: the lead carries it all. Kick and snare blip on the beats only
; (the hats are silent there), and `spkbass` fills the intro's hops and the
; breaths with the bass (only after 3+ silent sub-ticks, so the q1 gap between
; notes stays a clean articulation). Every pattern starts each channel from
; its `voice` and v12, so the lead phrases say v13, B's say @glock, and the
; chords say v10, each at its own start.

song fairway "Fairway"
groove 8 6
unit 16
rows 32
measure 16
spkbass
voice lead recorder
voice bass pluckbass
voice chord harp

; --- the intro: the ball tapped onto the green, over A7 - D7 ------------------
lead LI = v13 o5 e8 r16 a16 r8 >c+8 r16 <b16 a8 g8 e8 |
          d8 r16 <a16 r8 f+8 e8 f+8 a8 b16 >c16 |

; --- A: the theme ---------------------------------------------------------------
lead LA1 = v13 o5 d8 <b16 >d16&d8 g8 e8. d16 <b4 |
           >e8 <b16 >e16&e8 g+8 f+8. e16 d4 |
lead LA2 = v13 o5 c+8 <a16 >c+16&c+8 e8 g8. f+16 e4 |
           f+8 a8 >c4 <a4 r8 o4 b16 >c16 |
lead LA3 = v13 o5 c8 <a16 >c16&c8 e8 d8. c16 <a8 f+8 |
           g8 b8 >d8 e16 f+16 @chiparp g4. @recorder r8 |
bass BA1 = o2 g4 r8. d16 g4 d4 | e4 r8. <b16 >e4 g+4 |
bass BA2 = o2 a4 r8. e16 a4 e4 | d4 r8. <a16 >d4 e8 f+8 |
bass BA3 = o2 a4 e4 d4 <a4 | >g4 r8. d16 g4 d4 |
chord CA1 = v10 o4 r4 [d g b]4 r4 [d g b]4 | r4 [d g+ b]4 r4 [d g+ b]4 |
chord CA2 = v10 o4 r4 [e g >c+]4 r4 [e g >c+]4 | r4 [d f+ >c]4 r4 [d f+ >c]4 |
chord CA3 = v10 o4 r4 [e g >c]4 r4 [d f+ >c]4 | r4 [d g b]4 r4 [d g b]4 |
drum DA = k8 h8 s8 h16 h16 k8 h8 s8 h16 h16 | k8 h8 s8 h16 h16 k8 h8 s8 h16 h16 |
drum DF = k8 h8 s8 h16 h16 k8 h8 s8 h16 h16 | k8 h8 s8 h16 h16 T8. T16 t8 s8 |

; --- B: the bridge, on the glockenspiel over a half-time beat --------------------
lead LB1 = @glock v13 o5 g4 e8. g16 >c4 <g4 | d4 <b8. >d16 g4 f+4 |
lead LB2 = @glock v13 o5 e4 c8. e16 a4 g4 | f+8 e8 d8 c8 <a8 f+8 a8 b16 >c16 |
bass BB1 = o2 c4 r8. <g16 >c4 e4 | <b4 r8. g16 b4 >d4 |
chord CB1 = v10 o4 r4 [e g >c]4 r4 [e g >c]4 | r4 [d g b]4 r4 [d g b]4 |
chord CB2 = v10 o4 r4 [e g >c]4 r4 [e g >c]4 | r4 [d f+ >c]4 r4 [d f+ >c]4 |
drum DB = k8 h8 h8 h16 h16 s8 h8 h8 h16 h16 | k8 h8 h8 h16 h16 s8 h8 h8 h16 h16 |

order LI  BA2 CA2 DB          ; 0: the intro, A7 - D7
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 1: A  G E7 - the loop comes back here
order LA2 BA2 CA2 DF          ; 2:    A7 D7, the question
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 3: A' G E7
order LA3 BA3 CA3 DA          ; 4:    Am7 D7 G, the answer
order LB1 BB1 CB1 DB          ; 5: B  C G/B
order LB2 BA2 CB2 DF          ; 6:    Am7 D7, the run home
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 7: A' G E7
order LA3 BA3 CA3 DA          ; 8:    Am7 D7 G
loop 1
